            <ArticleTitle>Effects of nicorandil, an antianginal potassium channel opener, on left ventricular systolic and diastolic function in patients with chronic coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1685-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We compared the effects of nicorandil with nitroglycerin and nifedipine on left ventricular function. Intravenous nicorandil may be a balanced-typed vasodilator and useful in patients with left ventricular systolic and diastolic dysfunction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
